  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Cache Busting with Hashes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. The Problem",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Long TTLs make updates ==invisible== until expiry",
            "You **cannot** purge browsers, only your CDN",
            "Fix: put a content hash in the filename, e.g. `app.3f9a1c.js`",
            "New build means a new URL, so a cold fetch"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. How It Works",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Bundler hashes file **content** at build time",
            "HTML entry point references the hashed names",
            "HTML gets `no-cache` or a short TTL",
            "Assets get a year-long `immutable` TTL"
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "# hashed asset",
            "Cache-Control: public,",
            "  max-age=31536000, immutable",
            "# HTML entry point",
            "Cache-Control: no-cache"
          ],
          "note": "URL changes when content does"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Tool",
            "Hash token"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "webpack",
              "[contenthash]"
            ],
            [
              "Vite / Rollup",
              "[hash]"
            ],
            [
              "Next.js",
              "_next/static"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Example: Deploy",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "Build",
                "sub": "app.3f9a1c.js"
              },
              {
                "text": "Upload assets",
                "sub": "first"
              },
              {
                "text": "Publish HTML",
                "sub": "last"
              },
              {
                "text": "Keep old build",
                "sub": "avoid 404s"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Upload new assets first, then HTML: no missing file",
            "Keep previous assets so old HTML gets no 404",
            "Unchanged files keep URL and stay ==cached=="
          ],
          "style": "check"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Strategy",
            "Verdict"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Content hash",
              "Best: only changed files bust"
            ],
            [
              "Timestamp/version",
              "Busts everything each build"
            ],
            [
              "`app.js?v=2`",
              "Some proxies/CDNs ignore query"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Hashed asset with short TTL wastes the benefit",
            "Non-hashed asset with long TTL **traps** users on old files",
            "Shared chunk changes: every importer changes hash; split vendor code",
            "Never hash `sw.js`: a worker updates only from its fixed URL"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Cascading Hashes",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A hash covers a file's **content**, imports included",
            "Change a shared chunk and every importer rehashes",
            "Split ==vendor code== so it keeps its URL across builds"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "What changed",
            "Files rehashed"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "App code only",
              "App chunk"
            ],
            [
              "Shared chunk",
              "Every importer"
            ],
            [
              "Vendor (split out)",
              "None: stays cached"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Keep these short-lived",
          "text": "Serve `sw.js` and `manifest.json` with `no-cache`, never a year."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Rule of thumb",
          "text": "Hash it, cache it forever. No hash, no long TTL."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "nodedotjs",
      "subtitle": "Change URL, not TTL"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Misconfigurations and Cheatsheet",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Mistakes to avoid",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==HTML== with long `max-age`: users stay on the old release until expiry",
            "`no-cache` mistaken for `no-store`: **sensitive** data leaks into caches",
            "`Set-Cookie` on cacheable responses: CDN refuses, or caches one user's session",
            "Missing `Vary: Accept-Encoding`, or too broad `Vary: Cookie`/`User-Agent`"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Only `Last-Modified` behind load balancers: file times differ per server",
            "A CDN purge does **not** clear browser caches",
            "`Expires` and `max-age` disagree: max-age wins, debugging gets confusing",
            "Caching 5xx and soft 404s with the same long TTL as success"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Debug it",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "curl -I https://iolar.dev/app.css",
            "# Cache-Control: max-age=60",
            "# Age: 42        <- secs in cache",
            "# X-Cache: HIT   <- edge answered"
          ],
          "note": "-I sends HEAD, not GET"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "DevTools Network tab: size shows (memory cache) or (disk cache)",
            "That means no request left the browser",
            "`Age` above 0 means a shared cache answered",
            "`X-Cache: HIT/MISS` is the CDN's verdict"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
